{{also|Motley}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|motle}}, from {{der|en|xno|motteley||parti-colored}}, late 14th c., from {{der|en|ang|mot||speck}}, cognate with {{m|en|mote}}.

Equivalent to {{suf|en|mottle|y}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɒtli/}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|more|motlier}}

# Comprising greatly [[varied]] [[element]]s, to the point of [[incongruity]].
#: {{syn|en|heterogeneous|diverse|manifold|Thesaurus:heterogeneous}}
#* {{RQ:EHough PrqsPrc|II|0147|passage=Carried somehow, somewhither, for some reason, on these surging floods, were these travelers,{{nb...}}. Even such a boat as the ''Mount Vernon'' offered a total deck space so cramped as to leave secrecy or privacy well out of the question, even had the '''motley''' and democratic assemblage of passengers been disposed to accord either.}}
# Having many [[colour]]s; [[variegated]].
#: {{syn|en|colorful|prismatic|variegated|Thesaurus:multicolored}}

